// ============================================================================
//  mod_paralyzer.zone  -  BURIED'S PARALYZER, ON THE MAPS THAT CAN TAKE IT
//                                                                   (v2.17.35)
//  User, 2026-09-21/22: the Paralyzer in the box on every map it fits, and
//  ".give paralyzer" working off Buried.
//
//  SOURCE: every asset below is in zm_buried.ff, verified with Unlinker --list.
//  build_ff.bat already --load's zm_buried.ff, so nothing new is loaded and no
//  raw art of our own is needed - same as mod_blundergat.zone.
//
//  🛑 THIS GUN IS NOT LIKE THE BLUNDERGAT, and the difference is the whole
//  reason it took a second pass. The Blundergat is pure weapon file: its only
//  effects are muzzle flashes named as strings in the def, and a def's fx
//  string resolves leniently (this mod's Olympia has shipped on six maps for
//  weeks naming fx_shotgun_flash_base, a name in NONE of the six map zones).
//  The Paralyzer's behaviour is a SCRIPT, and maps\mp\zombies\_zm_weap_slowgun
//  ::init() calls loadfx() on seven weapon/paralyzer effects that exist only in
//  zm_buried.ff. A GSC loadfx is not lenient, and OpenAssetTools cannot read or
//  write FxEffectDef at all (retested 2026-09-22: --include-assets fx over a
//  map zone yields a zone file and zero effects), so those seven can never be
//  carried into mod.ff.
//
//  🌟 SO THE SCRIPT IS OURS, NOT THEIRS. scripts\zm\paralyzer.gsc is that init
//  re-implemented against effects this mod already ships as raw .efx inside
//  mod.iwd - the Winter's Howl freeze set, which loads on every map exactly
//  the way the T5 wonder weapons' 27 effects do. Read its banner for the
//  mapping. The core script is never called and never referenced: it lives
//  only in zm_buried.ff, so a qualified reference to it from a root script
//  would be an Unresolved external on every other map.
//
//  🛑 NOT ON ORIGINS, AND THE NUMBER IS WHY. The behaviour needs five
//  clientfields, 8 of them in the ACTOR set (slowgun_fx 3 + anim_rate 5).
//  Totalled from T6-Data-Archive\ZM\Clientfields with
//  awk '$1=="actor"{s+=$4}', stock actor bits are 31 of 32 on every zm_tomb
//  dump - one free. TranZit is 4-5, Die Rise 4-5, Nuketown 4, Mob 11-13, so
//  those clear it with room. Buried already ships the gun itself and is left
//  alone. The gate is in scripts\zm\boxfix.gsc and its client twin, and both
//  sides read the same map name.
//
//  📝 The defs ship raw in weapons\zm\ like every other ported gun -
//  slowgun_zm trimmed to fit the 20,480 runtime-loader ceiling, and
//  slowgun_upgraded_zm has been shipping there since v2.11.0 already.
//  camo_qol_slowgun and camo_slowgun are both in mod.ff today; the defs point
//  at the qol copy, which is what v2.11.0 authored for exactly this reason.
//  Both display strings, ZMWEAPON_PARALYZER and _UPGRADED, are in en_patch_zm
//  .ff - confirmed by dumping that zone's .str, not assumed.
// ============================================================================

// view / world models, stock and Pack-a-Punched
xmodel,t6_wpn_zmb_slowgun_view
xmodel,t6_wpn_zmb_slowgun_world
xmodel,t6_wpn_zmb_slowgun_upg_view
xmodel,t6_wpn_zmb_slowgun_upg_world

// all 12 view-model animations, in the zone's own order
xanim,viewmodel_paralyzer_idle
xanim,viewmodel_paralyzer_fire
xanim,viewmodel_paralyzer_pullout
xanim,viewmodel_paralyzer_putaway
xanim,viewmodel_paralyzer_quick_pullout
xanim,viewmodel_paralyzer_quick_putaway
xanim,viewmodel_paralyzer_sprint_in
xanim,viewmodel_paralyzer_sprint_loop
xanim,viewmodel_paralyzer_sprint_out
xanim,viewmodel_paralyzer_ads_fire
xanim,viewmodel_paralyzer_ads_up
xanim,viewmodel_paralyzer_ads_down
